2 CONT posted by Wm. Keith johnson from "Odland Family History" book 2.	Erik Odland: Erik in his younger days made several trips to the U.S.A.  Four of his mother's brothers had immigrated to the United States. On  his return to Norway, 
2 CONC he married and lived on a farm called Grastein  where the five oldest children were born. In March 1929 he sailed for  Canada, coming to the Enchant district. In and around this area he  had three brothers, many cousins, and acqua
2 CONC intances from the same  area in Norway. His wife and five children followed in October 1929.  The three younger children were born in the Sundial district. His wife  passed away in 1938. In 1944 he moved to a farm in the New West 
2 CONC  district. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Obit ENCHANT— (HNS) — Farmer in the Enchant district since 1929, Eric Odland died at to home there Tuesday following an Illness of two years, Mr. Odland was born in Norway, March 30, 1880, and came to the Enchant district in 1929.
2 CONC . His wife Abigail, whom he .married in Norway during 1917, died at Enchant in 1933. A member of the Evangelical Free Church at Enchant, he is survived by four sons, Sam, Peter, Erling and Alfred, all of Vauxhall four daughters, M
2 CONC rs. Johanna Severtson and Mrs. Christe Hagen, both of Enchant, Pauline and Arline, both at home; two brothers, Sam at Taber and John at Haney, B.C.; also five sisters in Norway. Funeral services will be held in the Evangelical Fre
2 CONC e Church at Enchant Friday at 2 p.m. Burial will be in the Enchant cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Publication: Lethbridge Herald April 4, 1951
2 CONT
2 CONT Odland immigration to Canada, prepared by William Keith Johnson, Ref: Odland Family History cira 1960. Skretting Family History 206-2007
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Odland Family History" book circa 1960" Anna Johanna Odland married Sem Erikson Skretting who changed his name to Odland. They lived on a farm adjacent to her parents. They raised ten children on t his small farm...Elen, '''
2 CONC Erik''', Sam, Sven, Tom and John immigrated to Canada. Tom returned to Norway. The descendants of the other four live in Canada. added by W.K.Johnson 
