1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Gards- og ættesoga for Hå, bind II, Odland, side 188, nr. 59.f, https://www.nb.no/items/URN:NBN:no-nb_digibok_2017012629002?page=191
2 CONT
2 CONT Submitted by WK Johnson:      Sam was a charter member of the 1st Evangelical Free Church in Canada at Enchant AB.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sam S. Odland Laid to Rest TABER—(HNS)— An old timer of Southern Alberta, Sam S. Odland of Taber, was laid to rest, in the Enchant cemetery Tuesday, following services conducted Monday evening in the Evangelical Free Church at Tab
2 CONC er, and Tuesday afternoon at the Evangelical Free Church at Enchant. Rev. L. W. Fosmark, Rev. C. Fosmark and Rev. Tony Hanson officiated at the services. Pallbearers were Arnold Odland, Sammy Odland, Tort Skretting, Robert Steen, 
2 CONC John Lind and Lloyd Hagen. Humphries Funeral Home of Taber, was in charge of arrangements. Mr. Odland was born Feb. 27, 1886, in Varhaug, Norway, emigrating in youth to Minnesota, and moving to the Enchant district in Southern Alb
2 CONC erta in 1906. He married Minnie Steen in 1916(WKJ note: married in Nov.1918, not 1916), and they resided at Enchant until retirement to Taber in 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Odland is survived by his widow, and five adopted children ( three from his brother Sven) a son Harold of Enchant, four daughters, Josephine ( Mrs. William Johnson), and Ionne (Mrs. Gudmind Skretting) of Enchant; Charlotte (Mr
2 CONC s. E. B. Peterson) of Scandia, and Miss Audrey at home, as well as 13 grandchildren. A brother John resides at Webster Corners, B.C., and four sisters remain in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Publication: Lethbridge Herald March 6, 1957 (with some corredctions by W.K. Johnson)
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription: Father Asleep in Jesus
2 CONT
